## Create cases

| Script | Usage summary | Purpose |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `bin/create-tec-batch.sh` | `<local-authority> [batch-type]` | Create one `TEC_BATCH` via `POST /batches`. No args shows help (unless `LOCAL_AUTHORITY` is set). Batch types: `registration`, `warrantAuthRequests`, `warrantReissueRequests`, `outOfTimeDecisions`, `changeOfAddress`, `caseClosureRequests`, `transferRequest` |
| `bin/create-tec-batches.sh` | `<count> [batch-type]` | Create many batches (rotates authority / type / state unless fixed). No args shows help |
| `bin/create-tec-case.sh` | `<batch-case-reference\|->` | Create one `TEC` PCN. The PCN comes from `generate-pcn-number.sh` using `LOCAL_AUTHORITY`'s TEC id (default Westminster `WE`), or from `PENALTY_CHARGE_NUMBER`. Pass `-` for no batch link; pass a batch ref (or `BATCH_CASE_REFERENCE`) to link the batch after create. A supplied PCN whose suffix is greater than `0` is also linked to the case for the preceding suffix |
| `bin/create-tec-cases.sh` | `<batch-case-reference\|->` | Bulk randomised PCNs (`CASE_COUNT`, default 20). Each PCN uses that case's TEC authority id |
| `bin/create-gm-tec-cases.sh` | `<batch-case-reference\|->` | PCNs for each Greater Manchester authority (`CASES_PER_AUTHORITY`, default 10), via `create-tec-case.sh` |
| `bin/create-tec-exception-case.sh` | (optional env overrides) | Create one `TEC_EXCEPTION` via `POST /exception-cases` |
| `bin/assert-batch-case-exists.sh` | `<batch-case-reference>` | Verify a CCD case exists and is `TEC_BATCH` (used by the create/link scripts) |
| `bin/generate-pcn-number.sh` | `<authority-id> [unique-number]` | Print a PCN (`AA9999999X0` or `AAA9999999X0`). Check digit is mod 11 of the authority id and the 7-digit number; suffix is always `0`. Omit the unique number to generate one |

### Create batch examples

```bash
./bin/create-tec-batch.sh westminster
./bin/create-tec-batch.sh westminster warrantAuthRequests
./bin/create-tec-batches.sh 6
./bin/create-tec-batches.sh 3 registration
LOCAL_AUTHORITY=manchesterCityCouncil ./bin/create-tec-batch.sh
```

Optional env overrides for batch create include `FILE_IDENTIFIER`, `BATCH_IDENTIFIER`,
`PCN_COUNT`, `OPERATION`, `RECEIVED_VIA`, `SUBMITTER_EMAIL`,
`TARGET_STATE` (`QUEUED_FOR_PROCESSING` | `PROCESSING_STARTED` | `PROCESSING_COMPLETE` | `PROCESSING_FAILED`),
and `ATTACH_SAMPLE_DOCUMENTS`.

`generate-pcn-number.sh` prints one PCN. `create-tec-case.sh` and `create-tec-cases.sh` call it
with the TEC id for the case's local authority (Westminster is `WE`). Format, letter values, and
the mod 11 check digit are on [Penalty charge numbers](/pcn-number.html). The worked example
`LR2468037` is `LR246803780`.

```bash
./bin/generate-pcn-number.sh LR 2468037
./bin/generate-pcn-number.sh WE
LOCAL_AUTHORITY=manchesterCityCouncil ./bin/create-tec-case.sh -
```

Set `PENALTY_CHARGE_NUMBER` to supply a PCN. File and batch identifiers then use that number's
authority id unless `FILE_IDENTIFIER` or `BATCH_IDENTIFIER` is set. When the supplied suffix is
greater than `0`, the script looks up the case for the immediately preceding suffix and links the
new case to it after create (`AB0531612A1` links to the case for `AB0531612A0`). The preceding
case must already exist, and there must be exactly one. The script exits before creating the PCN
if that lookup fails. Generated numbers always use suffix `0`, so they are not linked this way.
The link is a standard CCD case link (reason `CLRC007`, description "Previous registration").
`TecCaseView` returns the same predecessor on later reads, because CCD rebuilds `case_link` from
`caseLinks` on every save. Lookup uses the `tec` database (`DB_HOST`, `DB_PORT`, `DB_PASSWORD`,
or the local shared-database container when `psql` is not installed).

```bash
PENALTY_CHARGE_NUMBER=AB0531612A1 ./bin/create-tec-case.sh -
```

## Link and transition

| Script | Usage summary | Purpose |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `bin/link-pcn-to-batch.sh` | `<pcn-case-reference> <batch-case-reference>` | Loads batch operation; PCN `linkBatchCase` (`batchLinkCase` + `batchLinkType`, not Case details `batchCase`) then batch `linkPcnCases` (ExUI **linked to** / **linked from**). Registration sets `batch_case_reference`; other types use `tec_batch_pcn_link` without changing Case details **Batch case**. Additive: existing registration / Linked Cases links remain. Reason `OtherDescription` depends on the batch type. PCN state: `transferRequest` → `REFER_FOR_ENFORCEMENT`, `caseClosureRequests` → `CLOSED`, others unchanged |
| `bin/transition-to-case-issued.sh` | `<pcn-case-reference>` | Fire `registrationPaymentSucceeded` so a PCN reaches `CASE_ISSUED` |
| `bin/set-case-state.sh` | `<pcn-case-reference> <state>` | Fire `setCaseState` to jump a PCN to any `CaseState` (see [CCD architecture — States and events](/ccd-architecture.html#states-and-events)) |
| `bin/complete-batch-processing.sh` | `<batch-ref> <output-file-1> <output-file-2>` | Attach two Outputs documents and move a batch to `PROCESSING_COMPLETE` |

Link reason text (LOV `CLRC007` = Other) by batch type:

| Batch type | Default `OtherDescription` |
| --- | --- |
| `registration` | Linked as part of a batch of registrations |
| `warrantAuthRequests` | Linked as part of a batch of warrant auth requests |
| `warrantReissueRequests` | Linked as part of a batch of warrant reissue requests |
| `outOfTimeDecisions` | Linked as part of a batch of out-of-time decisions |
| `changeOfAddress` | Linked as part of a batch of change of address |
| `caseClosureRequests` | Linked as part of a batch of case closure requests |
| `transferRequest` | Linked as part of a batch of transfer requests |

Override with `BATCH_REGISTRATION_REASON`, `BATCH_WARRANT_AUTH_REASON`, and the other `BATCH_*_REASON` env vars, or `BATCH_LINK_REASON_CODE` for the LOV key.

A PCN may be linked to a registration batch and later to other batch types (e.g. warrant auth). Case details
**Batch case** stays on the registration batch; Linked Cases **linked from** lists each linked batch.

## Documents and applications

| Script | Usage summary | Purpose |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `bin/attach-case-file-document.sh` | `<case-ref> <folder> <file-path>` | Upload via Case Document AM and attach to Case File View. PCN folders by default. For batches: `CASE_TYPE_ID=TEC_BATCH EVENT_ID=attachBatchDocument` and folder `inputs` / `outputs` (payload field `batchFileDocument`) |
| `bin/generate-application.sh` | `<case-ref> <in\|out of time> <TE9\|PE3>` | `recordApplication`, fill PDF, attach under Applications |
| `bin/generate-time-extension.sh` | `<case-ref> <TE7\|PE2>` | `recordTimeExtension`, fill PDF, attach under Applications |
| `bin/enter-general-application.sh` | `<case-ref> <local authority\|respondent>` | `enterGeneralApplication` — uploads `N244_0622.pdf` and records an Issued general application. The event files the N244 under Applications and leaves PCN state unchanged. Clerk user (`tec-demo@test.com`) |
| `bin/apply-warrant-authorisation.sh` | `<case-ref>` | `applyWarrantAuthorisation` — appends a warrant authorisation (issue/expiry/status) to the PCN; `STATUS=active` → `WARRANT_AUTHORISATION_ISSUED`, `expired` → `WARRANT_AUTHORISATION_EXPIRED`, `cancelled` → state unchanged |

Optional env for a general application: `APPLICATION_TYPE` (`adjourn` \| `set aside` \| `something else`; default `something else`), `DATE_RECEIVED` (YYYY-MM-DD, default yesterday), `SOMETHING_ELSE_DETAILS` (default `OOT refusal appeal`), `WITHIN_14_DAYS` (`yes` \| `no`), `FEE_AMOUNT` (pence, default `12600` — £126.00), `APPLIED_FOR_HWF`, `HWF_REFERENCE`, `ALL_PARTIES_AGREE`, `WITHOUT_NOTICE`, `N244_FILE`. The fee is always recorded as received.

Optional env for warrant authorisation: `DATE_OF_ISSUE`, `DATE_OF_EXPIRY` (YYYY-MM-DD),
`STATUS` (`active` \| `expired` \| `cancelled`; default `active`). Defaults: issue = today,
expiry = today + 1 year.

## Runtime artefacts (not scripts)

These are created by the scripts and are gitignored / local-only:

- `bin/.venv-generate-application` — Python venv for PDF filling
- `bin/.local-dm-store-data/` — persisted dm-store binaries
- `bin/*.pid` / `bin/*.log` — process ids and logs for docs servers, nav proxy, and dm-store stub
- `design_docs/source/partials/_local_demo_case_links.html.erb` — output of `seed-demo-catalogue.sh` (live case refs; not committed)
- `bin/.demo-catalogue.json` — optional machine-readable dump of the last seed run
